{"id": "unknown-2026-07-05-004", "date": "2026-07-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 27, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Why countries are increasingly settling trade in local currencies", "content": "A growing number of economies seem to be exploring local-currency trade to lower transaction costs, limit exchange-rate risks, protect foreign-exchange reserves, and boost financial resilience. \nIndonesia-China and India-Sri Lanka are expanding such initiatives to strengthen financial resilience, conserve foreign exchange reserves and support more efficient cross-border payments. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/why-countries-are-increasingly-settling-trade-in-local-currencies-311465-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-05-005", "date": "2026-07-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 27, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India launches first domestically built EXIM container", "content": "India has unveiled its first domestically manufactured export-import shipping container for AP Moller-Maersk, marking a step towards strengthening local logistics and export supply chains. \nMaersk also ordered 1,000 more India-made containers from DCM Shriram Group. \nBacked by the Container Manufacturing Promotion Scheme, India aims to expand annual production capacity to 7,50,000 TEUs. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-launches-first-domestically-built-exim-container-311476-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-05-006", "date": "2026-07-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 27, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Germany’s apparel imports slightly higher in Q1, China’s share rises", "content": "Germany’s apparel imports continued to recover in Q1 2026, with sourcing shifting towards China, Vietnam and India.\nBangladesh and Türkiye lost market share despite remaining major suppliers.\nCotton garments and knitwear dominated imports, indicating buyers continue to prioritise competitive pricing, reliable supply and established sourcing networks.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/germany-s-apparel-imports-slightly-higher-in-q1-china-s-share-rises-311451-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
